{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3425","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3425","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3425\",\"parent_revision\":\"46ef739b6780f032a4bb100a2a304bc9edb8a7c11bc32f4f271d19c46b9b53c3\",\"root_revision\":\"46ef739b6780f032a4bb100a2a304bc9edb8a7c11bc32f4f271d19c46b9b53c3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSix sites in dh construct a dispatch prompt by hand-authoring the full text inline, rather than using the SAM one-liner or referencing the shared delegation template. The counted inventory is at `.tmp/scratch/reports/20260906-dh-dispatch-call-site-inventory.md`.\\n\\nInline-prompt sites, verified 2026-09-06:\\n- skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md:156 \u2014 dh:contract-verification\\n- skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md:185 and :226 \u2014 dh:task-worker\\n- skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md:30 and :73 \u2014 dh:backlog-item-groomer\\n- skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md:21 \u2014 dh:task-worker\\n\\nFor contrast: `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md:38` uses the SAM one-liner, and one file in dh contains an `OBSERVATIONS:` block (skills/verify-done/SKILL.md). `skills/kage-bunshin/SKILL.md` spawns through `tmux send-keys` with literal prompt strings \u2014 a separate mechanism no prompt-shape change would reach.\\n\\nThis item is deliberately filed as Ideas, not as agreed work. A prior session's claim of \\\"around eight sites hand-authoring full delegation templates\\\" was repeated from an unverified scout report and was wrong in both directions; the inventory above replaces it.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: unclear, and that is the point. Each inline prompt is independently maintained, so a change to delegation guidance reaches none of them \u2014 but no defect has been traced to this, and no consumer is known to be misled by it.\\n\\nGrooming must first answer: what goes wrong if these stay as they are? If that question has no concrete answer with a failure path, close this as wontfix rather than refactoring for uniformity.\\n\\nHard constraint: gates go on outcomes, never on prompt shape. PR #3422 deletes the repo-level validate-delegation hook; dh must not add a prompt-shape validator. Any change here is about authoring convenience and single-source-of-truth, never about enforcement.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: DH delegation-spine audit, session melodic-plotting-emerson (2026-09-06)\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"387cb8274c58188240ec3b538fac10a0a82a86d64eb0bfaf0b252a210d9e3e1a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSzTPjw\"}"}